<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Tudor returns four weeks after starting sertraline: one week at 25 mg, then 50 mg each morning for three weeks. The sore throat she had three weeks ago cleared within a week. She has had no nausea, diarrhea, headache, tremor, dizziness, or bruising and has missed no doses. Her first interpersonal psychotherapy session took place two weeks after the referral rather than in the first week, because private end-of-day sessions had to be found; she has now had three. She sleeps about five hours, keeps the sleep window, and rarely naps. She eats three small meals and the supplement twice a day. She has held two audiences this week and has begun to take some pleasure in the gardens again, though she still feels heavy most mornings. She has had no thoughts of death or of harming herself. The dentist has taken impressions for a new partial denture. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Medication</td><td>Sertraline 50 mg for three weeks after a week at 25 mg; no side effects</td></tr><tr><td>Psychotherapy</td><td>Three IPT sessions; the first was two weeks after referral</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>About five hours; Insomnia Severity Index 14</td></tr><tr><td>Function</td><td>Two audiences this week; some pleasure in the gardens</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>No suicidal thoughts</td></tr><tr><td>PHQ-9</td><td>13, down from 17</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

