    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Major depressive disorder, single episode, moderate (F32.1)</content>. PHQ-9 13, 24 percent below baseline, and GDS-15 8, after four weeks of sertraline and three weeks at 50 mg: early improvement, as expected at this point. Sodium 136 mmol/L, normal. No side effects; no suicidal thoughts. [S]<list><item>Continue sertraline 50 mg; review in three weeks.</item><item>If the PHQ-9 has not fallen by at least 50 percent after six to eight weeks at 50 mg, increase to 75 mg.</item><item>Continue weekly IPT.</item><item>Safety plan unchanged; 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline confirmed.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Acute viral pharyngitis (J02.9)</content>. Resolved within a week without antibiotics. [S]<list><item>No further action.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Chronic insomnia comorbid with depression (G47.00)</content>. Insomnia Severity Index 14, down from 19; sleep efficiency up on the diary. [S]<list><item>Widen the sleep window by 15 minutes, to 12:45 am to 6:30 am.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Fall risk (Z91.81)</content>. No falls; no orthostatic drop; Timed Up and Go 11 seconds. [S]<list><item>Continue the balance class.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Survey</td><td>PHQ-9</td><td>Baseline, then at least monthly during acute treatment; every 2 to 4 weeks in continuation</td><td>Completed today</td><td>13, down from 17 (24 percent); item 9 scored 0</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>GDS-15</td><td>Baseline and to monitor response in adults 65 or older (monthly here)</td><td>Completed today</td><td>8, down from 10</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Suicide risk reassessment (C-SSRS Since Last Visit and PHQ-9 item 9)</td><td>Every visit during active treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No suicidal thoughts, intent, plan, or behavior; PHQ-9 item 9 scored 0; safety plan unchanged</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Sodium after starting an SSRI in an older adult</td><td>About 2 to 4 weeks after starting</td><td>Completed today</td><td>136 mmol/L, normal</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>SSRI tolerability check two weeks after the dose change</td><td>2 weeks after starting and after each dose change</td><td>Deferred</td><td>Missed: the increase to 50 mg was made at the sick visit, and no contact was booked two weeks later; the first review at that dose is today, three weeks on. No harm: she has had no side effects, falls, or bleeding, and sodium is normal. Corrective action: a nurse telephone check is now booked two weeks after every antidepressant dose change</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Adherence and adverse-effect review</td><td>Every visit during active treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No missed doses; no nausea, headache, tremor, dizziness, or bruising</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Interpersonal psychotherapy</td><td>Weekly from referral</td><td>Deferred</td><td>Late start: the first session was two weeks after the referral, not within the first week, because private end-of-day sessions had to be found. Outcome: three sessions so far, and the PHQ-9 is falling. Corrective action: the clinic now holds two end-of-day psychotherapy slots each week for patients who need privacy</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Weight and nutrition</td><td>Every visit while weight is below her usual</td><td>Completed today</td><td>52.3 kg, up 0.2 kg from the last visit; supplement twice a day</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Fall risk on an SSRI: orthostatic blood pressure, gait, and falls since the last visit</td><td>At baseline, after starting an SSRI, and with dose changes</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No falls; no orthostatic drop; Timed Up and Go 11 seconds</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Sleep (CBT-I), activity, and social contact</td><td>Every visit during active treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Insomnia Severity Index 14; sleep window widened; two audiences held; walks most days</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Lithium, anticonvulsant, or antipsychotic monitoring (levels, metabolic tests, AIMS)</td><td>Only on those drugs</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Treated with an SSRI only</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Medical causes of low mood and weight loss excluded by the second visit. Outcome by 2026-01-26: Blood count, metabolic panel, calcium, albumin, TSH, vitamin B12, folate, and MoCA normal; diphenhydramine stopped [S]</item><item>Response (PHQ-9 down by at least 50 percent) by twelve weeks of treatment, then remission (PHQ-9 below 5). In progress; target 2026-04-20 [S]</item><item>No passive or active suicidal thoughts. Outcome by 2026-01-26: Passive death wish at intake only; PHQ-9 item 9 scored 0 from the second visit [S]</item><item>Sleep at least six hours most nights without hypnotics. In progress; target 2026-04-20 [S]</item><item>Weight back to at least 55 kg, with a comfortable denture. In progress; target 2026-06-15 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: APA Clinical Practice Guideline for the Treatment of Depression Across Three Age Cohorts (2019); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Major Depressive Disorder (2022); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monograph (2026); American Geriatrics Society 2023 Updated AGS Beers Criteria for Potentially Inappropriate Medication Use in Older Adults (2023); Management of Chronic Insomnia Disorder in Adults: A Clinical Practice Guideline From the American College of Physicians (2016)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Depression review in three weeks; her wellness visit is booked for next week. Next scheduled visit 2026-03-02: subsequent annual wellness visit. [S]</paragraph></text>

